WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.580
This infographic shows the overarching
document that governs these practices,

2
00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:09.280
the European Code of Conduct. This code is
a framework integrated directly

3
00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:11.820
into EU systems to ensure compliance.

4
00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:15.480
It acts as the definitive standard for
research ethics committees,

5
00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:19.020
principal investigators, and researchers
evaluating proposals.

6
00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:23.120
Strict adherence to this code maps out
clear boundaries for international data

7
00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:27.220
transfers and prevents the cascading
failures seen in the peer review process.

8
00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:32.460
Research integrity functions as a
rigorous, testable, operational standard

9
00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:36.460
that must be deliberately engineered into
every step of the scientific

10
00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:37.116
workflow.
